Modifications from upstream
----------------------------

Per Apache License 2.0 section 4(b), files changed from the original are
noted here:

- modeling_moss_audio.py: changed `from src.configuration_moss_audio import
  ...` to `from .configuration_moss_audio import ...` (a relative import),
  so the module resolves inside this vendored package
  (boo-moss-audio/vendor/moss_audio/) instead of requiring a top-level `src`
  package on sys.path.

- modeling_moss_audio.py: in `MossAudioEncoder._encode_chunk_batch`,
  `x = layer(...)[0]` was changed to check whether the WhisperEncoderLayer
  call returned a tuple before indexing. Upstream assumes
  `WhisperEncoderLayer.forward` returns `(hidden_states, attn_weights)`,
  which was true on the transformers version upstream was written against.
  transformers >=4.51's `WhisperEncoderLayer.forward` returns the
  hidden-state tensor directly (`-> torch.Tensor`), so unconditional `[0]`
  indexing silently sliced off the first batch element instead of
  unpacking a tuple, corrupting every encoder layer after the first.

- modeling_moss_audio.py: rewrote `MossAudioModel.prepare_inputs_for_generation`
  to delegate the standard input-slicing/attention-mask/position-id
  bookkeeping to `GenerationMixin.prepare_inputs_for_generation` (via
  `super()`) instead of upstream's hand-rolled `cache_position[0] > 0`
  check. transformers >=4.51's `generate()` drives slicing via a
  `next_sequence_length` kwarg and no longer threads an updated
  `cache_position` through `model_kwargs` between decode steps, so
  upstream's check always saw prefill state, never sliced `input_ids`
  down to the newest token on decode steps, and kept re-including the
  prefill-length `audio_input_mask` against a growing `input_ids`/
  `inputs_embeds`, causing a shape-mismatch crash in `forward` on the
  first decode step. The rewritten version uses the base
  implementation's `is_first_iteration` flag (passed correctly by
  `generate()`) to gate the audio-specific kwargs instead. No other
  changes.

All other files are unmodified copies of the upstream source.
